  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "If $n$ is a positive integer, prove that $\\binom{2n}{n}$ is even.\n\nHint: Consider pairing the choices.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Every selection pairs with its distinct complement, so $\\binom{2n}{n}$ is even.",
      "worked": "There are $\\binom{2n}{n}$ ways to choose $n$ objects from a set of $2n$ distinct objects. Pair each selection with the selection of the other $n$ objects.\n\nTaking the complement twice returns the original selection, so every selection belongs to exactly one pair. Since $n\\geq1$, a selection and its complement are distinct. Thus the selections occur in pairs, and $\\binom{2n}{n}$ is even.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
